\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hardware Overview
\f1\b0 \
The car is built around the 
\f0\b Particle Photon
\f1\b0 , which serves as the central microcontroller. The Photon handles all sensor input, motor control logic, and cloud communication over its built-in Wi-Fi connection.\

\f0\b Locomotion
\f1\b0  is handled by two 
\f0\b continuous rotation servo motors
\f1\b0 , one for each drive wheel. These are controlled through the 
\f0\b DRV8835 dual motor driver carrier
\f1\b0 , which allows the Photon to vary speed and direction on each motor independently. This gives the car the ability to drive forward, reverse, and turn by varying the relative speed of each wheel.\

\f0\b User input
\f1\b0  comes from a 
\f0\b 2-axis joystick
\f1\b0 , which is read by the Photon's analog input pins. The X-axis controls steering (differential speed between left and right motors) and the Y-axis controls forward/reverse throttle.\

\f0\b Lap detection
\f1\b0  is handled by an 
\f0\b HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor
\f1\b0  mounted at the front of the car. When the car passes a reflective marker or wall at the start/finish line, the sensor registers the distance drop and triggers a lap event in the firmware.\

\f0\b Visual feedback
\f1\b0  is provided by a 
\f0\b flexible WS2812B RGB LED strip
\f1\b0  mounted on the chassis. After each lap, the LEDs flash green if the car beat its previous best time, red if it was slower, and cycle through a rainbow animation if a new record is set. A 
\f0\b 16x2 I2C LCD display
\f1\b0  shows live stats \'97 current speed estimate and last lap time \'97 while the car is running.\

\f0\b Data logging
\f1\b0  is done entirely through the Particle Cloud. After each lap event, the Photon publishes the lap number, lap time, and estimated velocity using 
\fs26 Particle.publish()
\fs24 . This data is pulled by the web dashboard in real time using the Particle Cloud API.\
All components are mounted on a 
\f0\b custom 3D-printed chassis
\f1\b0  designed to securely hold the servo motors, Photon, breadboard, and sensor array while keeping the center of gravity low for better handling.\
